``` NotC2: AWS-Native AI C2 Proof of Concept
    Field names follow CIM/UDM conventions and have not been tested against live data; adjust them to your environment.
    Splunk hunt over raw events, for data not mapped to CIM. Author: daniyyell-dev. https://github.com/daniyyell-dev/rapid-threat-intel/tree/main/threats/2026-11_November-2026/2026-11-10/NotC2-AWS-Native-AI-C2-Proof-of-Concept
    Sources: https://www.varonis.com/blog/notc2-ai-powered-c2-channel
    Define the rti_network, rti_dns, rti_web and rti_endpoint macros once (example: all/splunk_macros.conf).
    Each macro takes one argument, a list of search terms used to pre-filter the raw events, and must only use
    streaming commands (search, eval, rename, rex, fields, spath) so it can run inside multisearch.
    Set the time picker to at least the last 30 days. The indicators below are live and malicious.
    Output: first_seen, last_seen, ioc, ioc_type, data_model, host, user, src, dest, detail, count

    Behaviours (indicators of attack) are extra sections below, with ioc_type "behaviour (alert)" or "behaviour (hunt)".
    Behaviours are leads, not confirmed indicators, and can match legitimate activity. Compare any hit against your own baseline and environment before acting.
    Behaviours are for hunting and alerting only; never block on them.
    Sections that read raw logs use index=*: replace it with your own index names to make them faster. ```
``` Behaviour 1 (Alert): SNS subscription to an external HTTP(S) endpoint by a Lambda role
    Look for: SNS Subscribe with protocol http or https, made by a Lambda execution role (assumed-role session, often with exec-env/AWS_Lambda in the user agent)
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (sns.amazonaws.com), or CloudAppEvents with the AWS connector
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventSource="sns.amazonaws.com" eventName="Subscribe" requestParameters.protocol IN ("http", "https")
| eval host=coalesce(recipientAccountId, 'userIdentity.accountId'), user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), src=sourceIPAddress, dest=coalesce('requestParameters.endpoint', "-"), detail="Subscribe ".coalesce('requestParameters.topicArn', "-")." UA: ".coalesce(userAgent, "-")
| fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
| stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
| eval data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
| eval ioc="SNS subscription to an external HTTP(S) endpoint by a Lambda role", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"

``` Behaviour 2 (Hunt): SNS subscription confirmed for a new external endpoint
    Look for: SNS ConfirmSubscription for a new external HTTP or HTTPS endpoint
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (sns.amazonaws.com)
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventSource="sns.amazonaws.com" eventName="ConfirmSubscription"
    | eval host=coalesce(recipientAccountId, 'userIdentity.accountId'), user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), src=sourceIPAddress, dest=coalesce('requestParameters.topicArn', "-"), detail="ConfirmSubscription UA: ".coalesce(userAgent, "-")
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | eval ioc="SNS subscription confirmed for a new external endpoint", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 3 (Hunt): SNS topic created by a Lambda role
    Look for: SNS CreateTopic called by a Lambda execution role
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (sns.amazonaws.com)
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventSource="sns.amazonaws.com" eventName="CreateTopic" userAgent="*exec-env/AWS_Lambda*"
    | eval host=coalesce(recipientAccountId, 'userIdentity.accountId'), user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), src=sourceIPAddress, dest=coalesce('requestParameters.name', "-"), detail="CreateTopic from a Lambda runtime"
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | eval ioc="SNS topic created by a Lambda role", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 4 (Alert): New SQS-to-Lambda trigger
    Look for: New SQS-to-Lambda event source mapping (CreateEventSourceMapping with an SQS queue ARN)
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (lambda.amazonaws.com)
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventSource="lambda.amazonaws.com" eventName="CreateEventSourceMapping*" requestParameters.eventSourceArn="*:sqs:*"
    | eval host=coalesce(recipientAccountId, 'userIdentity.accountId'), user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), src=sourceIPAddress, dest=coalesce('requestParameters.functionName', "-"), detail="SQS source ".coalesce('requestParameters.eventSourceArn', "-")
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | eval ioc="New SQS-to-Lambda trigger", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 5 (Alert): Queue, function and trigger created by one identity within an hour
    Look for: One identity calling sqs:CreateQueue, lambda:CreateFunction and lambda:CreateEventSourceMapping within an hour
    Log source: CloudTrail management events
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventName IN ("CreateQueue", "CreateFunction*", "CreateEventSourceMapping*")
    | eval user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), step=case(match(eventName, "^CreateQueue"), "CreateQueue", match(eventName, "^CreateFunction"), "CreateFunction", 1==1, "CreateEventSourceMapping")
    | bin _time span=1h
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen dc(step) AS steps values(sourceIPAddress) AS src BY user _time
    | where steps=3
    | eval host="-", src=mvjoin(src, ","), dest="-", detail="CreateQueue, CreateFunction and CreateEventSourceMapping in the same clock hour", data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | fields - steps _time
    | eval ioc="Queue, function and trigger created by one identity within an hour", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 6 (Alert): AWS resources named NotC2
    Look for: SQS queue named NotC2-Commands, or queue, function or topic names containing NotC2
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (sqs CreateQueue requestParameters.queueName), AWS CLI command lines on endpoints
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" "NotC2"
    | eval host=coalesce(recipientAccountId, 'userIdentity.accountId'), user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), src=sourceIPAddress, dest=coalesce('requestParameters.queueName', 'requestParameters.functionName', 'requestParameters.name', "-"), detail=eventName." with a NotC2 name"
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | eval ioc="AWS resources named NotC2", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]
| append [
    search `rti_endpoint(NotC2)`
    | where match(process, "(?i)notc2")
    | eval host=dest, user=user, src="-", dest=dest, detail=coalesce(parent_process_name, "-")." > ".coalesce(process, process_name, "-")
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="endpoint"
    | eval ioc="AWS resources named NotC2", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 7 (Hunt): First Bedrock use by a Lambda role
    Look for: Bedrock InvokeModel, Converse or ConverseStream from a Lambda execution role that has not used Bedrock in the previous 30 days
    Log source: CloudTrail management events (bedrock.amazonaws.com)
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" eventSource="bedrock.amazonaws.com" eventName IN ("InvokeModel", "InvokeModelWithResponseStream", "Converse", "ConverseStream") userIdentity.type="AssumedRole"
    | eval user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), lambda=if(like(userAgent, "%exec-env/AWS_Lambda%"), "Lambda user agent; ", "")
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen values('requestParameters.modelId') AS models values(lambda) AS lambda values(sourceIPAddress) AS src BY user
    ``` first Bedrock call by this role falls in the last 7 days of the search window; run over 30 days or more ```
    | where first_seen >= relative_time(now(), "-7d@d")
    | eval host="-", src=mvjoin(src, ","), dest="bedrock.amazonaws.com", detail=mvjoin(lambda, "")."new Bedrock caller; models ".mvjoin(mvindex(models, 0, 4), ", "), data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | fields - models lambda
    | eval ioc="First Bedrock use by a Lambda role", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 8 (Hunt): Lambda role calling Bedrock and discovery APIs together
    Look for: The same Lambda role calling Bedrock and broad discovery APIs (ec2 DescribeInstances, dynamodb ListTables, rds DescribeDBInstances, lambda ListFunctions, s3 ListBuckets) in the same hour
    Log source: CloudTrail management events
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" userIdentity.type="AssumedRole" eventName IN ("InvokeModel", "Converse", "ConverseStream", "DescribeInstances", "ListTables", "DescribeDBInstances", "ListBuckets", "ListFunctions*")
    | eval user=coalesce('userIdentity.sessionContext.sessionIssuer.arn', 'userIdentity.arn'), is_model=if(match(eventName, "^(InvokeModel|Converse)"), 1, 0), discovery=if(is_model=0, eventName, null())
    | bin _time span=1h
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen sum(is_model) AS model_calls dc(discovery) AS disc values(discovery) AS discovery BY user _time
    | where model_calls>0 AND disc>=2
    | eval host="-", src="-", dest="-", detail=model_calls." model calls; ".mvjoin(discovery, ", "), data_model="aws:cloudtrail"
    | fields - model_calls disc discovery _time
    | eval ioc="Lambda role calling Bedrock and discovery APIs together", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]

``` Behaviour 9 (Alert): Bedrock function named execute_aws_operation
    Look for: A Bedrock tool definition named execute_aws_operation, or prompts starting with "ai:"
    Log source: Bedrock model invocation logs (CloudWatch Logs or S3); not in CloudTrail
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* "execute_aws_operation"
    | eval host=host, user=coalesce(user, "-"), src=coalesce(src, src_ip, "-"), dest=sourcetype, detail=substr(replace(_raw, "\s+", " "), 1, 300)
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="Bedrock invocation logs"
    | eval ioc="Bedrock function named execute_aws_operation", ioc_type="behaviour (alert)"
]

``` Behaviour 10 (Hunt): Lambda logs relaying commands through SNS
    Look for: Lambda log lines "SNS message body:" followed by Command:, Target:, Exit Code:, Output: and Error: fields, or functions configured with SNS_TOPIC_ARN or SNS_TOPIC_NAME
    Log source: Lambda CloudWatch Logs and function configuration
    Lead, not proof: compare any hit with your own baseline before acting. ```
| append [
    search index=* "SNS message body:"
    | eval host=host, user=coalesce(user, "-"), src=coalesce(src, src_ip, "-"), dest=sourcetype, detail=substr(replace(_raw, "\s+", " "), 1, 300)
    | fillnull value="-" host user src dest detail
    | stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY host user src dest detail
    | eval data_model="Lambda logs"
    | eval ioc="Lambda logs relaying commands through SNS", ioc_type="behaviour (hunt)"
]
| sort 0 - last_seen
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table first_seen last_seen ioc ioc_type data_model host user src dest detail count

``` Behaviours to check by hand (no reliable Splunk field mapping, so no search is written):

    Behaviour 11 (Hunt): Full SQS to Lambda to Bedrock to SNS command chain
        Look for: An SQS message from an unexpected source, then a Lambda run, Bedrock calls, other AWS API calls and an SNS publish to an external subscriber within minutes, all on the same queue, function and topic
        Log source: CloudTrail data events (SQS, Lambda, SNS), SNS delivery-status logs, Bedrock invocation logs
        Why no search: needs CloudTrail data events for SQS, Lambda and SNS correlated over minutes on one request chain; review the chain by hand from any hit above

    Behaviours are leads, not confirmed indicators, and can match legitimate activity. Compare any hit against your own baseline and environment before acting. Behaviours are for hunting and alerting only; never block on them. ```
``` Other hunt leads (not network or hash indicators), check manually:
    [other] NotC2
    [other] execute_aws_operation ```
``` Behavioural hunt notes:
    Look for new or unexpected SQS-to-Lambda event source mappings (lambda:CreateEventSourceMapping).
    Look for Bedrock InvokeModel or Converse calls from a Lambda execution role that has not previously used Bedrock, especially if that role also starts calling unrelated AWS APIs.
    Look for SNS HTTP or HTTPS subscriptions to external endpoints created by a Lambda execution role.
    Correlate an unexpected SQS message, a Lambda invocation, Bedrock activity, downstream AWS API calls and an SNS publish to an external subscriber in a short window. ```
